fc=json.loads((B/"AUTHORITY-FUNCTION-CLASSES.json").read_text())
fc["slot_discovery_law"]={'definition': 'Every current authority-capable reference is independently extracted and must be explicitly classified or fail ambiguous. Authority roles use source-bound structured declarations, exact schema semantics, then local predicates; never a key-name allowlist.', 'roles': ['AUTHORIZING_DESIGNATION', 'DIAGNOSTIC_DECLARATION', 'HISTORICAL_STATEMENT', 'MENTION', 'AMBIGUOUS_CURRENT_REFERENCE'], 'authority_tokens': ['authoritative', 'authorizing', 'authority', 'refuses', 'refusal', 'refusing', 'decides', 'derived by', 'derives', 'evaluated by', 'enforces', 'governs', 'controls', 'determines', 'adjudicates', 'authorizes', 'blocks', 'permits', 'certifies', 'rejects', 'establishes', 'gates', 'validates', 'loader'], 'class_tokens': ['DIAGNOSTIC', 'diagnostic', 'NON_AUTHORIZING', 'non-authorizing', 'PROVISIONAL_UNTIL_M3'], 'history_tokens': ['formerly', 'historically', 'was then'], 'clause_law': "A claim is read ONLY from the clause containing the reference. Clauses break at '.', ';', ':', ',' and newline, at parenthesis depth zero, and only where the delimiter is followed by whitespace or the end of the text - so an argument list, a dotted module path and a version number stay intact while ordinary punctuation ends a clause. Wrapped markdown prose is rejoined into logical lines first, so where a line happens to wrap cannot change a classification.", 'negation_law': "Negation is LOCAL, never a phrase search. 'X is no longer authoritative; Y is authoritative' classifies X non-authorizing and Y authorizing, because each clause is read separately. No bare negation appears in any token list: the v1.16 scanner exempted any sentence containing the phrase 'no longer', and in the TOCTOU law that phrase modified 'the bundle's binding no longer resolves' - an unrelated clause - which suppressed a real diagnostic-name violation (V116-B1).", 'signal_precedence': ["an explicit class or history token in the reference's OWN clause", 'the structured key path (a key whose name declares diagnostic/provisional/authorizing)', "the authority verbs of the reference's own clause"], 'reference_forms': ['bare', 'module-qualified', 'anchor (module.py#name)', 'path-qualified (tools/module.py#name)', 'markdown code (`name`)', 'call form name(args)'], 'module_awareness': 'A same-named function in another module is a DIFFERENT symbol: evidence_authoring.derive_attachment_state is the AUTHORIZING authoring wrapper, not the diagnostic authority_lib core function, and is recorded as a foreign-module symbol rather than judged against the authority_lib class map.', 'laws': {'R1': 'every reference to a demoted function in a CURRENT artifact carries an explicit class token in its own clause', 'R2': 'every clause that designates authority names a function whose canonical class is authorizing'}, 'artifact_scope': 'derived from AUTHORITY-PRECEDENCE.json: status STILL_ACTIVE and role in (NORMATIVE_AUTHORITY, CORRECTION_RECORD). Never a filename pattern. GENERATED_EVIDENCE (the validation report and the generated inventory) reports what the suite checked and quotes its own check names, so it is out of scope by published role; HISTORICAL_INPUT is out of scope by status.', 'generated_inventory': 'AUTHORITY-SLOT-INVENTORY.json', 'generator': 'tools/authority_slots.py, used by both this build and validate_v1_18.py', 'reference_metadata': 'AUTHORITY-REFERENCE-METADATA.json', 'document_universe': 'AUTHORITY-DOCUMENT-UNIVERSE.json', 'ambiguity_law': 'AMBIGUOUS_CURRENT_REFERENCE fails validation; current decision-function MENTION is allowed only for an explicitly foreign module symbol.'}
dump("AUTHORITY-FUNCTION-CLASSES.json",fc)
